    情 | qíng | emotion; sentiment
    象 | xiàng | phenomenon; aura
    象 | xiàng | image; manifestation

semantic_boundary_contrasts:
  core_nuance: 气氛 denotes the psychological, emotional, or social ambience prevailing in a shared space.
  contrasts[3]{id,compared_word,pinyin,analysis}:
    1 | 气氛 vs. 环境 | huánjìng | 环境 refers to objective physical conditions, surroundings, or ecology, whereas 气氛 describes intangible emotional ambience.
    2 | 气氛 vs. 气候 | qìhòu | 气候 denotes meteorological weather patterns over decades, while 气氛 is the psychological tone of a gathering.
    3 | 气氛 vs. 心情 | xīnqíng | 心情 is an individual's private emotional state, whereas 气氛 is collective and shared across a group or venue.

extended_reading_passages[2]{id,hanzi,pinyin,en,es}:
  #1 | 春节期间的大街小巷张灯结彩，到处弥漫着浓郁喜庆的年节气氛。爆竹声声伴随着清脆的欢笑，邻里之间互致吉祥问候，那一份份淳朴热烈的情感，在冬日暖阳的照耀下汇聚成最动人的社会温情画卷。 | Chūnjié qījiān de dàjiē-xiǎoxiàng zhāngdēng-jiécǎi, dàochù mímàn zhe nóngyù xǐqìng de niánjié qìfēn. Bàozhú shēngshēng bànsuí zhe qīngcuì de huānxiào, línlǐ zhījiān hùzhì jíxiáng wènhòu, nà yífènfèn chúnpǔ rèliè de qínggǎn, zài dōngrì nuǎnyáng de zhàoyào xià huìjù chéng zuì dòngrén de shèhuì wēnqíng huàjuàn. | During Spring Festival, streets were adorned with lanterns and festive streamers, suffused with celebratory holiday cheer. Firecrackers popped alongside laughter as neighbors exchanged blessings, weaving a moving tapestry of community warmth. | En Año Nuevo chino, las calles lucían farolillos entre una atmósfera festiva y entrañable. Petardos y risas se fundían con parabienes vecinales, conformando bajo el sol invernal un cálido tapiz de afecto social.
  #2 | 篮球场上火热的竞技气氛，最忌讳被频繁机械的停顿所扑灭。早年因为桃筐未掏空底部，每次投篮进球后观众都必须百无聊赖地看着工人们踩梯取球，原本紧张刺激的比赛气氛瞬间变得索然无味。锯掉筐底的巧思，真正挽救了这项运动的灵魂活力。 | Lánqiúchǎng shang huǒrè de jìngjì qìfēn, zuì jìhuì bèi pínfán jīxiè de tíngdùn suǒ pūmiè. Zǎonián yīnwèi táokuāng wèi tāokōng dǐbù, měicì tóulán jìnqiú hòu guānzhòng dōu bìxū bǎiwú-liáolài de kàn zhe gōngrénmen cǎi tī qǔ qiú, yuánběn jǐnzhāng cìjī de bǐsài qìfēn shùnjiān biàn de suǒrán-wúwèi. Jù diào kuāngdǐ de qiǎosī, zhēnzhèng wǎnjiù le zhè xiàng yùndòng de línghún huólì. | The fiery atmosphere of the basketball court suffers most from mechanical interruptions. In early years, because peach baskets lacked open bottoms, fans boredly watched workers climb ladders after each score, deflating the thrilling mood. Sawing open the bottom truly salvaged the sport's electric soul. | El fervor de la pista de baloncesto se marchita con parones mecánicos. Al inicio, las canastas ciegas forzaban al público a contemplar cómo se bajaba el balón con escaleras, apagando la pasión. Abrir el fondo rescató el alma vibrante del juego.
